Backport of ml-explore/mlx#4554 ("[CUDA] Add gather_qmm_rhs_sm80", merged
2026-10-01): a sorted-rhs gather_qmm for fp modes (nvfp4, mxfp4, mxfp8) on
sm_80+, the CUDA twin of Metal's gather_qmm_rhs.

- GatherQMM ran qmm_sm80 with one block per (token, expert) pair on grid z:
  each pair was a one-row tile, and past 65,535 pairs (an 8192-row chunk at
  top-10) the launch failed with "invalid argument". The sorted kernel runs
  each expert's rows as one group (grid z = 1).
- It carries upstream's fix to qmm_sm80_mainloop issuing cp.async past the
  last K tile.

The quantized.cpp hunk is rebased onto mlx-cuda-qmm-read-weights-once.patch.
Drop this file and its step in build-mlx-linux.sh once lib/mlx-src includes
the upstream commit.

